params.description3:
{{sbc|Innate - Wolf:}} Starting at {{sbc|2:53}}, '''Wolf''' periodically marks a random large {{tip|monster}} within the enemy team's jungle for 180 seconds. The ''hunted'' camp is highlighted on the [[Map (League of Legends)|mini map]] to both teams. Once the ''hunted'' target is slain or the mark expires, '''Wolf''' will wait 45 seconds before selecting a new target. <br/>The type of monster that '''Wolf''' can mark changes based on '''Kindred's''' current ''Mark of the Kindred'' stacks:
* {{sbc|0 :}} {{ui|Rift Scuttler}}
* {{sbc|1 – 3:}} {{ui|Rift Scuttler}}, {{ui|Crimson Raptor}}, {{ui|Gromp}}
* {{sbc|4 – 7:}} {{ui|Ancient Krug}}, {{ui|Blue Sentinel}}, {{ui|Greater Murk Wolf}}, or {{ui|Red Brambleback}}
* {{sbc|8 + :}} {{ui|Rift Herald}} or {{ui|Baron Nashor}}, {{ui|Dragon}} or {{ui|Elder Dragon}}

params.notes:
* ''Dance of Arrows'' has no minimum dash range.
{{always quickcast}}
* The {{sti|cooldown}} will not be modified if it cannot be reduced (the current cooldown would have to be less than the reduction amount in this case).

* ''Mounting Dread'' cannot target small {{tip|monsters}}.
* If the target becomes {{tip|untargetable}}, {{tip|death|dies}}, or is too far away or no longer in {{tip|sight}} during the cast time, this ability will cancel and not pay its cost but still go on {{sti|cooldown}}.{{bug}}
* This ability cannot target a unit with ''Mounting Dread'' stacks.
* ''Mounting Dread'' will prioritize casting on the closest champion within {{tip|cr|icononly = true}} {{tt|100|estimated}} radius of the cursor, even if other eligible targets are closer.
** As a consequence of this mechanic, ''Mounting Dread'' can still be cast on champions with ''Mounting Dread'' stacks.{{bug}}
*** Reapplying ''Mounting Dread'' through this method will apply the slow, but will not reset the stack count.
* {{pending for test}} Reapplying ''Mounting Dread'' against {{ai|Inherent Glamour|Neeko|disguised}} {{ci|Neeko}} will reset the stack count.{{bug}}
